25,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing our internal experts and the crews aren't sticking to standard training. We need a vendor that provides heavy, on-site support.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Our hardware is a mess and the peak season is a total blackout for changes. We can't afford a rigid cutover.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The board prefers operating costs over capital, but separate licenses are bleeding us dry over time. We need price stability.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Last winter was a disaster because no one owned the outage. Also, our rules change too fast for a frozen scope.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,We have a habit of skipping upgrades and inheriting messy data from external teams. We need something sustainable and clean.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, does that mean you prefer an internal team or a very high-quality partner?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, if the scope can't be frozen, we need a system that is flexible on the fly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, if support is scattered, a bundled suite might be the only way to ensure a single point of contact.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree. A single vendor for everything would stop the finger-pointing we saw last winter.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, I suspect a partner firm might just repeat the 2018 data lift mistakes. I'd prefer a vendor with skin in the game.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, that makes sense. If the vendor is present during rollout, the depot supervisors might actually adopt the system.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just don't want another tool that gets replaced by spreadsheets because it can't handle our actual yard devices.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,We should avoid modular licensing. The renewal invoices show that separate add-ons are where the costs spiral.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Yumi,,So we need a hosted suite or a single-vendor solution that can adapt to rule changes quickly.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. A system that ages in place is a liability. We need a clear path for updates.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"It sounds like we all want a vendor that is deeply integrated into our actual operations, not just a software provider.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"Right, someone who understands that November to January is a no-go zone for big changes.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Toshio,,And someone whose pricing is predictable and bundled.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm looking for accountability and flexibility.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests we avoid the ""partner firm"" model if we want to avoid the 2018 disaster.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
