50,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D has an engineering team present through rollout. That solves my concern about the supervisors and the staffing gap.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Candidate D is built specifically for transport operators. That sounds like it would actually survive our yards.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate B is a hosted suite with a fixed configuration. That might be stable, but D is on our own servers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Candidate B has a regional service team, which helps with ownership, but D's on-site presence is even better.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D avoids the external partner risk of C and the modular cost traps of A. It's the most rational choice.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, would the on-premise nature of D be a problem for the board's capital requests?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, do you think D can handle the rule changes better than B's fixed configuration?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"The board is trimming capital, but a single outright purchase for D might be cheaper than B's recurring fees.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, D's engineering team being on-site means they can adjust the rules as we go, unlike B's fixed process.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"D is the only one that addresses the ""aging in place"" issue by having the engineers here to maintain it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm convinced. D is the safest bet for our people.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki. D fits the depot reality.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"If it avoids the modular price creep of A, I can support D.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I agree. The on-site team provides the accountability I'm looking for.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The evidence points to D as the most robust solution for our specific failures.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Let's vote.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
